# CODEOWNERS — Foundation repo
# Adopter customisation: replace every placeholder handle below with real GitHub handles.
#
# Rules enforced (the CDR process's Approval checklist, Leadership Forum
# cadence, and branch protection/CODEOWNERS — one canonical rule):
# 1. No single human may satisfy two required-reviewer slots on the same PR.
#    Combined with branch protection's "proposer cannot approve" rule.
# 2. Sensitive substrate paths require Admin + Leader (two-approver).
# 3. Canonical reviewer-set rule: Leader + Domain Lead of each affected domain
#    (+ Product Owner and Admin where the CDR template lists them).
#    CODEOWNERS cannot express "affected domains" or "PO of the affected
#    domain", so it lists the fallback superset below; the PR-template
#    Approval checklist records the actual affected set and PO sign-off,
#    and a CI check (Task 4, codeowners-lint / checklist-complete) fails
#    the PR if the checklist is incomplete.

# Default: any unmatched file
*                                @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader

# Two-approver substrate (harness-level changes).
# Deadlock fallback ("Small-org fallback to the multi-hat rule"):
# when the Admin authors a /standards/ PR and cannot self-approve the Admin
# slot, a Domain Lead countersigns in Admin's place.
/standards/                      @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.github/workflows/              @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.github/hooks/                  @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.github/agents/                 @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/         @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.claude/                        @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/CLAUDE.md                       @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/AGENTS.md                       @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/FORMATS.md                      @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader
/.mcp.json                       @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader

# Cross-domain coupling: Leader + all Domain Leads + Admin
# (Adopters narrow to the actually-affected Domain Leads per-PR via the
#  PR-template Approval checklist; this list is the CODEOWNERS fallback
#  superset. Admin is included here because the CDR template asserts an
#  Admin sign-off — CODEOWNERS previously silently dropped it. Product
#  Owners are NOT listed here: CODEOWNERS cannot express "PO of the
#  affected domain" — PO sign-off is recorded via the PR-template Approval
#  checklist instead.)
/interfaces/                     @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader @placeholder-domain-1-lead @placeholder-domain-2-lead @placeholder-domain-3-lead @placeholder-domain-4-lead
/cross-domain-decisions/         @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader @placeholder-domain-1-lead @placeholder-domain-2-lead @placeholder-domain-3-lead @placeholder-domain-4-lead
/architectural-decisions/        @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader @placeholder-domain-1-lead @placeholder-domain-2-lead @placeholder-domain-3-lead @placeholder-domain-4-lead
/nfrs/                           @placeholder-admin @placeholder-leader @placeholder-domain-1-lead @placeholder-domain-2-lead @placeholder-domain-3-lead @placeholder-domain-4-lead

# Glossary: 1 Leader + Admin (substrate, lower-stakes than standards).
# Affected-domain routing note: a shared-term change is notified to, but not
# blocking on, the affected Domain Lead(s) — CODEOWNERS cannot express
# "affected domain" for a cross-domain glossary entry; use the PR-template
# Approval checklist to record which Domain Lead(s) reviewed.
/glossary.md                     @placeholder-leader @placeholder-admin

# Templates (lower-stakes substrate).
# Affected-domain routing note: same as /glossary.md above — template
# changes are notified to affected Domain Leads via the Approval checklist,
# not added here as blocking CODEOWNERS reviewers.
/standards/templates/            @placeholder-leader @placeholder-admin

# References (patterns library)
/references/                     @placeholder-admin
